  "goodToKnow": "Der Groschen was a coin: in West Germany, colloquially the 10-pfennig piece, and in Austria one hundredth of a schilling, until the euro arrived in 2002. It survives in idioms: Der Groschen ist gefallen (the penny dropped), keinen Groschen wert (worthless), and der Groschenroman (pulp novel). The name comes from Latin grossus (thick), a large silver coin. The plural is the same: die Groschen."
